      "message": "Will this produce desired behavior when wakeup_reasons changes in the middle of the for loop due to a second suspend/resume cycle?\n\nThis could partially be addressed by move-assigning wakeup_reasons to a local vector and iterating over that.\n\nBut there would still need to be a mutex around the move assignment _from_ wakeup_reasons to be truly robust, which means the same lock would have to be held around the assignment _to_ wakeup_reasons in notifyWakeup.  Those are both minuscule sections of code for locking, but it would still be preferable if notifyWakeup() didn\u0027t do any blocking at all, if there\u0027s a better solution that accomplishes that.",
